{"response": "In Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback (RLHF), a frozen reference model is one that remains unchanged during the training process of an AI agent. This means the model's parameters or structure do not evolve based on feedback from human evaluators throughout the training sessions. Instead, it focuses on refining its own policies to match those observed behaviors over time, eventually learning how to interact effectively with humans without further adjustments from the human trainers. This approach allows for self-learning systems while maintaining consistency across different rounds of interaction.", "response_token_ids": [641, 46069, 10927, 20909, 448, 11097, 36857, 320, 4728, 49716, 701, 264, 19690, 5785, 1614, 374, 825, 429, 8458, 34857, 2337, 279, 4862, 1882, 315, 458, 15235, 8315, 13, 1096, 3363, 279, 1614, 594, 5029, 476, 5944, 653, 537, 37580, 3118, 389, 11055, 504, 3738, 19326, 2973, 6814, 279, 4862, 15704, 13, 12090, 11, 432, 23497, 389, 73185, 1181, 1828, 10186, 311, 2432, 1846, 13166, 27099, 916, 882, 11, 9583, 6832, 1246, 311, 16282, 13444, 448, 12677, 2041, 4623, 32974, 504, 279, 3738, 50091, 13, 1096, 5486, 6147, 369, 656, 70756, 5942, 1393, 20337, 28137, 3941, 2155, 19531, 315, 16230, 13, 151645], "response_length": 102, "terminated_with_eos": true, "reached_generation_ceiling": false, "row_index": 9, "prompt_id": "wl10", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Explain what a frozen reference model does in RLHF in at most 45 words."}], "prompt_tokens": 48, "rendered_prompt_sha256": "c6c708c0c6b0dc6b6bc700e67b2b6121965a9b0b32693b36fa0e06dc04c69e25", "policy_token_logp": [-0.5210180282592773, -0.7511166334152222, -0.00047755756531842053, -9.250213042832911e-05, -0.3518903851509094, -0.08266747742891312, -0.01906920224428177, -0.004047298803925514, -0.00010418349120300263, -8.153582894010469e-05, -0.024930281564593315, -0.03852948173880577, -0.025405962020158768, -0.004360097460448742, -0.0038290531374514103, -0.7347361445426941, -1